# ==============================================================================
# SECRETS — 30 §2 / §18.3 · 31 §19.5
# ==============================================================================
# Until now this file had NO secret pattern at all. Only `env/` and `venv/`
# matched a grep for "env", and those are virtualenv DIRECTORIES, not secret
# files. Verified before this change — every one of these would have been
# committed by a single `git add -A`:
#     active_token.txt  .env  .env.local  token.txt  secrets.json
#     credentials.json      -> all "WOULD BE COMMITTED"
#
# That gap is why the reference implementation's `active_token.txt` (a live
# session token stored in plaintext beside the code) was rejected rather than
# adopted: the repo had no net beneath it.
#
# .connect/tools/secret_scan.py scans file CONTENT and its own remediation
# advice is "add .env to .gitignore" — which had never been done. Content
# scanning and ignore rules are complementary, not substitutes: the scanner
# catches a secret pasted into tracked source, these rules stop a secret FILE
# from being tracked at all.
#
# NOTE: the patterns below are deliberately anchored to real secret-bearing
# filenames. `secret_scan.py` itself is tracked tooling and must NOT be
# ignored — verified with `git check-ignore` after this change.

# Environment / credential files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.template
!.env.sample

# Token & session material (incl. the reference script's active_token.txt)
# NOTE: `*_token.txt` alone does NOT match a bare `token.txt` — the glob needs
# at least one character before the underscore. Verified: `token.txt` came back
# "COMMITTABLE" until `*token.txt` was added. Both spellings are kept so the
# intent stays readable.
active_token.txt
*token.txt
*_token.txt
*.token
token.json
tokens.json

# Credential stores
credentials.json
*credentials.json
secrets.json
*secrets.json
*.secret

# Keys & certificates
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*

# Provider account pools / session dumps
accounts_*.json
session_dump*.json
cookies.json
cookie_jar.json
